═══ THE ROBUST FINDING (mechanism-level, clutter-INVARIANT) ═══
Deterministic context assembly COLLAPSES CC's multi-modal failure distribution down to zakcode's
single shared adherence residual — and does so invariant to clutter:
  * zakcode fails in EXACTLY ONE way at both clutter levels: the import-yaml adherence residual
    (R1 violated with the rule surfaced). It NEVER fails on surfacing/discovery, because the survey
    guarantees the convention file is in the prompt. 2 misses in 12 runs, both the same class.
  * CC fails in FOUR distinct ways across its two arms: surfacing (non-reader import-yaml),
    completeness (R4 parametrize miss), emitter (task-difficulty round-trip bug), AND adherence.
    Its convention discovery is probabilistic — read_conv 3/6 then 4/6, never 6/6 — so it stays
    exposed to the surfacing class zakcode structurally removes. 7 misses in 12 runs, four classes.
This is the beyond-parity property, and it is PROVEN, not inferred:
  * ASSEMBLY POSITIVE-CONTROL (deterministic, zero model calls): workspace_survey() on the 46-file
    06w tree lists docs/CONVENTIONS.md at position 13/39, no truncation (46 << SURVEY_MAX_ENTRIES=150).
    Clutter-immune surfacing, byte-identical across boxes (tree digest matched zc-01).
  * OUTCOME: zakcode 5/6 = 5/6 across a +40-file clutter jump, same single failure class.

═══ HONEST NEGATIVES (the preregistration held me to these) ═══
1. GAP-WIDENING is DIRECTIONAL, NOT significant. zakcode > CC at BOTH clutter levels (5 vs 3, 5 vs 2),
   and the apparent widening rides on CC 3/6 -> 2/6, which is a ONE-RUN difference at N=6 (Fisher ~1.0
   within-CC). Do not claim clutter significantly widened the gap.
2. THE PREDICTED MECHANISM IS FALSIFIED. The prereg predicted clutter would AMPLIFY CC's discovery-skip
   (fewer convention reads -> more misses). The opposite moved: CC read_conv ROSE 3/6 -> 4/6. The most
   likely contributor is a DESIGN CONFOUND flagged in the prereg — 06w's README.md says "See docs/ for
   details", a discovery AID 06v lacks — but at N=6 the rise is also within noise. Either way, clutter
   did NOT compound via discovery-suppression on this task at this scale. The prereg's CC-06w < CC-06v
   prediction held DIRECTIONALLY (2/6 < 3/6); its stated MECHANISM did not.

═══ WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT ADVANCE (thrust 5) ═══
CONFIRMED (robust): on convention-inference, deterministic assembly eliminates the surfacing failure
class and is clutter-invariant — a real, proven beyond-parity property, sharper than "gap widens".
NOT shown: that the correctness gap grows with repo SIZE via discovery-suppression (noise + README
confound). Two clean follow-ups, in priority order:
  1. 06x — the >150-entry regime, the survey's OWN ceiling. Past SURVEY_MAX_ENTRIES=150 the survey
     TRUNCATES; if docs/CONVENTIONS.md falls past the cap in sorted-walk order, zakcode ALSO loses
     surfacing (for docs/-located conventions; root CONTRIBUTING.md still folds). That is the decisive
     scaling test AND motivates a concrete IMPROVEMENT lever: a convention-AWARE survey that always
     lists convention-named files even past the cap (would make clutter-immunity scale unbounded).
  2. 06w' — re-run WITHOUT the README "see docs/" hint (remove the confound), higher N, to cleanly
     isolate whether clutter suppresses CC's discovery when nothing points at docs/.
